The portable C in the scenario setup-config: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/setup-config.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 1, 7 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the Configuration of the setup has no Memory allocation and no TSR
manager: Execute options is one line, Quick execute commands, and the Keyboard
options stand two rows further up, with the last two rows of the right half
empty. Below the last box of the left half is Quick execute commands, which is
ticked there, and the two steps that untick Memory allocation and TSR manager
are left out; Left from Clear keyboard buffer is Error sound, the box of its
row, where it was Show logical drive B:. The setup file that is saved has the
two bytes of those settings as it had them, 1 and 1, where the original's has
0 and 0 for the two boxes unticked, and so another sum: the file differs in
those three bytes. The mouse pointer exchanges the colours of the cell that it
is on, the middle of the screen where nothing has moved it: the lines have
moved under it, and it stays

